--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
dropped the body of function
--
N5008 [temp.inst]/1-3: instantiating istream<char> instantiates its base
ios<...>, whose typedef num_put<out_iter<char>> leads to out_iter's
typedef naming ostream<char>.  Neither typedef requires a complete class,
but the front end instantiated the classes they name: ostream<char> was
instantiated while ios<...> had only its ios_base members and kept that
partial member list, so `this->np' in insert was an "unresolved member
expression" and insert's body was dropped (bin53).  Member typedefs no
longer instantiate the class they name (test_typedef_uses.desc covers
uses that do).  This was the drop of basic_ostream::_M_insert in
libstdc++'s <sstream> (cpp11_libstdcxx_header_drops/test_ostream_int).
g++ 13 and clang++ 18 accept this program, and it fails only its WRONG
assertion.
